text.section:
To be entitled to compensation from a manufacturer under this subsection, the dealer shall:

Employ watercraft and engine parts expressly authorized by the manufacturer for warranty work;


Retain a copy of the manufacturer's then current service literature, if any;


Record the warranty work with the manufacturer within forty-five days of completing the warranty work;


Complete and maintain for inspection by the manufacturer, a manufacturer's delivery checklist signed by the customer for each watercraft or watercraft engine sold by the dealer;


Promptly handle all warranty work in accordance with industry standards regardless of the location where the watercraft or watercraft engine was sold; and


Submit warranty registration cards to the manufacturers on a timely basis.
